bio=section('<div class="biography-layout"><article><p class="source-note">Artist-supplied biography on the official Mr. Blindbandit website. This is not a Wikipedia article.</p><p class="large-copy"><strong>Kaeleb Savon Heck</strong> (born April 4, 2000), professionally known as <strong>Mr. Blindbandit</strong>, is an American recording artist, producer, creator, and founder of Blindbandit Records.</p><p>Blind since birth, Heck has developed a creative identity around music, independent production, accessibility, and digital media. His public work includes ambient, cinematic, electronic, dreamcore, and hip-hop releases, alongside video and personal storytelling.</p><nav class="bio-contents" aria-label="Biography contents"><a href="#early-life">Early life &amp; perspective</a><a href="#career">Music career</a><a href="#label">Blindbandit Records</a><a href="#family">Family</a><a href="#sources">Sources &amp; external links</a></nav><h2 id="early-life">EARLY LIFE &amp; PERSPECTIVE</h2><p>Heck has roots in Virginia, USA, and a home in the Philippines. He identifies as blind since birth and uses screen readers and accessible technology as part of his creative work. His public channels share both music and the experience of life as a blind creator.</p><h2 id="career">MUSIC CAREER</h2><p>Under the Mr. Blindbandit name, Heck releases music across several styles and formats. The catalog includes Sapphire castles, Genesis, The eternal bloom, weightless, and cry forever. Singles, albums, and EPs appear alongside extended and dreamscape versions of earlier ideas.</p><p>Credited creative connections include UUu Tang Maskman, Yxngfery, Pablo Jackson Hairston, R3NJ1, true_explores, and Trukidchris. The site’s collaborator pages link to the shared work rather than implying label membership.</p><h2 id="label">BLINDBANDIT RECORDS</h2><p>Heck founded Blindbandit Records as part of his independent creative practice. The label portal connects the artist’s music with submission information and professional inquiries. His wider creative identity also includes Mr. BlindBandit Studios, video, and digital storytelling.</p><h2 id="family">FAMILY &amp; PERSONAL STORY</h2><p>In the family details supplied for this biography, Heck names his daughter Madeline Heck, his mother Celyne Heck, his sister Kelsey Heck, and his brother Christopher Andrew Hall Jr. This page includes their names without additional personal or contact details.</p><h2 id="sources">SOURCES &amp; EXTERNAL LINKS</h2><p>The birth date and family names on this page were supplied by Kaeleb for his own website. Music titles and creative credits are linked to official streaming catalogs. This biography does not claim independent encyclopedic verification.</p><ul><li><a href="'+SPOT+'">Mr. Blindbandit on Spotify</a></li><li><a href="'+APPLE+'">Mr. Blindbandit on Apple Music</a></li><li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@MrBlindbandit">Official YouTube channel</a></li><li><a href="/credits/">Selected music credits</a></li></ul></article><aside class="bio-infobox"><img src="/assets/artist.jpg" alt="Kaeleb Savon Heck, known as Mr. Blindbandit" width="531" height="640" loading="lazy"><dl><dt>Name</dt><dd>Kaeleb Savon Heck</dd><dt>Artist name</dt><dd>Mr. Blindbandit</dd><dt>Born</dt><dd>April 4, 2000<br><small>Artist-supplied</small></dd><dt>Creative work</dt><dd>Recording artist, producer, creator</dd><dt>Label</dt><dd>Blindbandit Records</dd><dt>Roots / home</dt><dd>Virginia / Philippines</dd></dl></aside></div>')
publish('/biography/','Kaeleb Savon Heck biography','THE ARTIST / BIOGRAPHY','KAELEB<br><span>SAVON HECK.</span>','The life and creative work of Mr. Blindbandit.',bio)

